# L §6.1 joints, nested (E §3.1 step 1: "a member that is itself a joint model pins its own members through its use
# lines"): f is a joint model of a and d whose own party ania is a's and d's Ania by its same lines; the outer model
# joins f's ania and b's Ania, `same f.ania = b.ania`.  f's own name ania is a name f declares (its entry in
# fam_cast), so the outer model reads it as f.ania, the one thing f's same lines made of it.  q1: f's own figure,
# Ania's parts at a and d (600.00, scratch/nested/mk_nested.py); q2, q3: b's pot holds 70.00 of Ania's, read as f.ania
# or b.ania (carried through).  (Was LOAD-SAME "same f.ania = b.ania: a field path and a thing": f's join renamed its
# own ania to its member's, and the outer model lost the name; the probe writer's pair/family.)
=== options pin=bytes
=== j.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30
  use b = "hb.tally" sha256 "60a1c4098cc69b5635048da5abe1e95ef9e3aff77350f28408ec0d4e345b6633"
  use f = "fam.tally" sha256 "7b64f7833415e5f8ee8e434f304de60f2a216327383418edbb79085390891870"
  same f.ania = b.ania

ask q1: f.ania_parts[2026-06-30]
ask q2: bal(b.pot, 2026-06-30) of f.ania
ask q3: bal(b.pot, 2026-06-30) of b.ania
=== fam.tally
model fam
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30
  use a = "ha.tally" sha256 "ee0df750f773e1f31d7dc054aa039d0738c44c34246a8aa951ea57e2cd3301d0"
  use d = "hd.tally" sha256 "1c70ec565b0d3c12a5e0405f7217c90fb914543113d186387e631dbb10478f71"
  same a.ania = ania
  same d.ania = ania

source fam_papers "who is who"

def ania_parts[t in days]: money DUK = bal(a.sav, t) of ania + bal(d.dep, t) of ania

ask q_fam: ania_parts[2026-06-30]

version fam_cast
  cite fam_papers
  known 2026-01-01
  parties + [ania] lives 1988-04-12..
=== ha.tally
model pa
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source papers "papers"
unit DUK: currency minor 0.01
kind inheritances: transfers
  attr heir: key parties
kind savings: place DUK min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(DUK)
  takes k for w prorata ties by (if k.owner == ania then 0 else 1)
place sav: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input rows: observed
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule inherited = (if p == m.heir then 1 else 0) when m in inheritances

version cast
  cite papers
  known 2026-01-01
  parties + [ania] lives 1988-04-12..
  parties + [tomek] lives 1960-01-01..

version recs
  cite papers
  governs 2026-01
  known 2026-02-03
  rows[r1] = (on: 2026-01-05, kind: inheritances, leg cash from world to sav amount 150.00 DUK, heir: tomek) "line 1"
  rows[r2] = (on: 2026-01-06, kind: inheritances, leg cash from world to sav amount 200.00 DUK, heir: ania) "line 2"
